                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17359019" author="ericgao888" created="Tue, 8 Jun 2021 03:20:50 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Is there a way this bug can be reproduced? I tried to corrupt the json from backend, seemed it would automatically reformat to a well-formatted json after running cells from the front-end. If I deleted the json from backend directly, it would disappear after refreshing the page from front-end. Can&apos;t find a way to trigger this &apos;Fail to parse note json&apos;. Could you please provide an example? Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17359020" author="theosardin" created="Tue, 8 Jun 2021 03:24:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Did you restart zeppelin after corrupting the json ? I think that&apos;s when it would happen, when zeppelin starts and the note is already corrupted. In terms of real life case for example, think of a zeppelin server that restarts daily and pulls from github, while someone made a change in the github directly that broke the note&apos;s json.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17359024" author="ericgao888" created="Tue, 8 Jun 2021 03:43:49 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Successfully reproduced the bug. Thx for the explanation.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
